{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 18, "model_name": "meta/llama-4-maverick-17b-128e-instruct", "content": "\"the social network\" is a thought-provoking film that delves into the fascinating story of facebook's creation and the tumultuous journey of its founder, mark zuckerberg. directed by david fincher, the movie is a gripping narrative that explores the complexities of ambition, friendship, and the consequences of success.\n\nthe film begins with mark zuckerberg, a sophomore at harvard, being dumped by his girlfriend, erica albright. in a state of anger and hurt, mark creates a website called \"facemash\" that allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive. the site becomes an instant hit, but also generates controversy and gets mark into trouble with the university.\n\nsoon after, mark is approached by twin brothers, cameron and tyler winklevoss, who propose an idea for a social networking site exclusively for harvard students. mark agrees to work on the project, but eventually becomes more interested in creating his own site, which he calls \"thefacebook.\" with the help of his friend eduardo saverin, mark launches the site, and it quickly gains popularity.\n\nas facebook's user base expands, mark and eduardo's friendship becomes strained due to their differing visions for the site. meanwhile, the winklevoss twins claim that mark stole their idea and sue him for intellectual property theft.\n\nthe film's narrative is presented in a non-linear fashion, jumping back and forth between different periods in mark's life. this structure allows the audience to piece together the events that led to the creation of facebook and the subsequent lawsuits.\n\nthe cast delivers impressive performances, with jesse eisenberg standing out as the complex and enigmatic mark zuckerberg. eisenberg's portrayal captures mark's intelligence, ambition, and social awkwardness, making him a relatable and intriguing character. andrew garfield also shines as eduardo saverin, bringing a sense of vulnerability and naivety to the role.\n\nthe film's themes are multifaceted and open to interpretation. on one hand, \"the social network\" is a cautionary tale about the dangers of unchecked ambition and the consequences of prioritizing success over relationships. on the other hand, it's also a commentary on the elitism and exclusivity of harvard and the privileged class.\n\nthe cinematography is sleek and modern, capturing the sterile, high-tech atmosphere of the facebook headquarters and the luxurious surroundings of harvard. the score, composed by trent reznor and atticus ross, is equally impressive, adding a layer of tension and unease to the narrative.\n\noverall, \"the social network\" is a captivating film that offers a nuanced and thought-provoking exploration of the facebook phenomenon. it's a movie that will appeal to anyone interested in technology, entrepreneurship, and the complexities of human relationships.", "logprobs": [{"token": "\"", "logprob": -0.617240309715271}, {"token": "the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " social", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "\"", "logprob": -1.0728830375228426e-06}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -8.22540732769994e-06}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " thought", "logprob": -0.6815173029899597}, {"token": "-prov", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "oking", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.015212936326861382}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.002477435627952218}, {"token": " delves", "logprob": -0.2050515115261078}, {"token": " into", "logprob": -2.861018856492592e-06}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " fascinating", "logprob": -0.5193052291870117}, {"token": " story", "logprob": -0.002683611586689949}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.004078404977917671}, {"token": " facebook", "logprob": -0.0007995745982043445}, {"token": "'s", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {